{"schemaVersion":1,"corpusId":"euclid-elements-heath-1908","status":"raw_machine","contentItem":{"id":"euclid-10-59","kind":"proposition","title":"性质与证明：二项无理线段与中项无理线段与无理线段","englishTitle":"If an area be contained by a rational straight line and the sixth binomial, the side of the area is the irrational straight line called the side of the sum of two medial areas.","book":10,"number":59,"status":"raw_machine","sourceMissing":false,"source":{"urn":"urn:cts:greekLit:tlg1799.tlg001.perseus-eng2:10.prop_2.59","url":"https://scaife.perseus.org/reader/urn:cts:greekLit:tlg1799.tlg001.perseus-eng2:10.prop_2.59/","group":"prop_2","sourceNumber":59,"corpusSha256":"ba12e2e47aec41f853ff32929a2d0467926f93280f1bf8870bda5016c29d143c","hasSourceFigure":true,"historicalChineseUrl":null}},"revision":{"id":"euclid-10-59@raw-f0a9a345d616d972","contentId":"euclid-10-59","version":1,"status":"raw_machine","contentHash":"f0a9a345d616d972ea61e7a292ff7f46f0e1e61f080885f379558a6137a25fbf","createdBy":"mathforge-corpus-import","changeSummary":"Imported Heath source and machine-assisted Chinese draft. No mathematical or editorial review is implied.","blockIds":["euclid-10-59.statement","euclid-10-59.construction.1","euclid-10-59.construction.2","euclid-10-59.proof.1","euclid-10-59.proof.2","euclid-10-59.proof.3","euclid-10-59.proof.4","euclid-10-59.proof.5","euclid-10-59.proof.6","euclid-10-59.proof.7","euclid-10-59.proof.8","euclid-10-59.construction.3","euclid-10-59.construction.4","euclid-10-59.proof.9","euclid-10-59.conclusion","euclid-10-59.source"]},"blocks":[{"id":"euclid-10-59.statement","contentId":"euclid-10-59","revisionId":"euclid-10-59@raw-f0a9a345d616d972","order":0,"kind":"statement","title":"命题陈述","status":"raw_machine","contentHash":"22bfb1d3cb21baa2c4998b72a4ffbb53e7d2d9dc881198fd0af515838545980a","citations":[],"surfaces":[{"id":"heath-en","role":"source","language":"en","status":"source_transcription","text":"If an area be contained by a rational straight line and the sixth binomial, the side of the area is the irrational straight line called the side of the sum of two medial areas."},{"id":"machine-zh","role":"machine_translation","language":"zh-CN","status":"raw_machine","text":"如果一个区域由有理线段和6 二项无理线段组成,则该区域一侧是无理线段个称为总面积为2 中项无理线段个区域的一侧。"}]},{"id":"euclid-10-59.construction.1","contentId":"euclid-10-59","revisionId":"euclid-10-59@raw-f0a9a345d616d972","order":1,"kind":"construction","title":"作图与构造 1","status":"raw_machine","contentHash":"569a19f648980b8ed64ec5aed7da9868c1fc2345cb438052eb7dbb38265b5837","citations":[],"surfaces":[{"id":"heath-en","role":"source","language":"en","status":"source_transcription","text":"For let the area ABCD be contained by the rational straight line AB and the sixth binomial AD, divided into its terms at E, so that AE is the greater term; I say that the side of AC is the side of the sum of two medial areas."},{"id":"machine-zh","role":"machine_translation","language":"zh-CN","status":"raw_machine","text":"ABCD区由有理线段 AB和6 二项无理线段 AD组成,分为E,因此AE是较大数目的;我说,AC是两个中项无理线段个区域之和的一边。"}]},{"id":"euclid-10-59.construction.2","contentId":"euclid-10-59","revisionId":"euclid-10-59@raw-f0a9a345d616d972","order":2,"kind":"construction","title":"作图与构造 2","status":"raw_machine","contentHash":"6f05b40f38e9703450a76b53958750b66bcf29a76d3f800c156ce3bcbe8c9bcd","citations":[],"surfaces":[{"id":"heath-en","role":"source","language":"en","status":"source_transcription","text":"Let the same construction be made as before shown."},{"id":"machine-zh","role":"machine_translation","language":"zh-CN","status":"raw_machine","text":"做同样的工程 之前显示。"}]},{"id":"euclid-10-59.proof.1","contentId":"euclid-10-59","revisionId":"euclid-10-59@raw-f0a9a345d616d972","order":3,"kind":"proof_step","title":"证明 1","status":"raw_machine","contentHash":"b4cec827ab1ebb3a9ec8767e75c95e06fcecd61f0099bcca974777b78e0354b6","citations":[],"surfaces":[{"id":"heath-en","role":"source","language":"en","status":"source_transcription","text":"It is then manifest that MO is the side of AC, and that MN is incommensurable in square with NO."},{"id":"machine-zh","role":"machine_translation","language":"zh-CN","status":"raw_machine","text":"由此可见,MO为AC,MN为正方形中的不可公度,NO为MO。"}]},{"id":"euclid-10-59.proof.2","contentId":"euclid-10-59","revisionId":"euclid-10-59@raw-f0a9a345d616d972","order":4,"kind":"proof_step","title":"证明 2","status":"raw_machine","contentHash":"485783e1b39dcdb04039068b94aa2d505add12151929cf5245572989f09fe3da","citations":["euclid-10-21"],"surfaces":[{"id":"heath-en","role":"source","language":"en","status":"source_transcription","text":"Now, since EA is incommensurable in length with AB, therefore EA, AB are rational straight lines commensurable in square only; therefore AK, that is, the sum of the squares on MN, NO, is medial. [[X. 21](/principles/euclid-10-21)]"},{"id":"machine-zh","role":"machine_translation","language":"zh-CN","status":"raw_machine","text":"现在,EA,长度不可公度,AB,有理线段,平方可公度而长度不可公度,有理线段,AB,AK,即MN的正方形,NO的中项无理线段。 [[X. 21](/principles/euclid-10-21)]"}]},{"id":"euclid-10-59.proof.3","contentId":"euclid-10-59","revisionId":"euclid-10-59@raw-f0a9a345d616d972","order":5,"kind":"proof_step","title":"证明 3","status":"raw_machine","contentHash":"ee10c56b92505cc07adfff4d550807f7fbdb8fc52540721c51c254db3f8d7539","citations":["euclid-10-13","euclid-10-21"],"surfaces":[{"id":"heath-en","role":"source","language":"en","status":"source_transcription","text":"Again, since ED is incommensurable in length with AB, therefore FE is also incommensurable with EK; [[X. 13](/principles/euclid-10-13)] therefore FE, EK are rational straight lines commensurable in square only; therefore EL, that is, MR, that is, the rectangle MN, NO, is medial. [[X. 21](/principles/euclid-10-21)]"},{"id":"machine-zh","role":"machine_translation","language":"zh-CN","status":"raw_machine","text":"同样,由于ED的长度为不可公度,为AB,因此FE的长度为不可公度的EK,为中项无理线段的FE,为有理线段的平方可公度而长度不可公度,因此,EL的长度为MR,即矩形的MN的NO,为中项无理线段。 [[X. 13](/principles/euclid-10-13)] [[X. 21](/principles/euclid-10-21)]"}]},{"id":"euclid-10-59.proof.4","contentId":"euclid-10-59","revisionId":"euclid-10-59@raw-f0a9a345d616d972","order":6,"kind":"proof_step","title":"证明 4","status":"raw_machine","contentHash":"69afb8a3ae59dc2c89decc9cef800d2293c3a297a6f714563157d20b607bc35f","citations":["euclid-6-1","euclid-10-11"],"surfaces":[{"id":"heath-en","role":"source","language":"en","status":"source_transcription","text":"And, since AE is incommensurable with EF, AK is also incommensurable with EL. [[VI. 1](/principles/euclid-6-1), [X. 11](/principles/euclid-10-11)]"},{"id":"machine-zh","role":"machine_translation","language":"zh-CN","status":"raw_machine","text":"AE是不可公度,EF,AK也是不可公度,EL [ [VI. 1](/principles/euclid-6-1) [X. 11](/principles/euclid-10-11)"}]},{"id":"euclid-10-59.proof.5","contentId":"euclid-10-59","revisionId":"euclid-10-59@raw-f0a9a345d616d972","order":7,"kind":"proof_step","title":"证明 5","status":"raw_machine","contentHash":"0b0afae62252459cc179c63a7b590b48918f9a032eab02a6bf181ee0cf092514","citations":[],"surfaces":[{"id":"heath-en","role":"source","language":"en","status":"source_transcription","text":"But AK is the sum of the squares on MN, NO, and EL is the rectangle MN, NO; therefore the sum of the squares on MN, NO is incommensurable with the rectangle MN, NO."},{"id":"machine-zh","role":"machine_translation","language":"zh-CN","status":"raw_machine","text":"但AK是MN,NO的正方形和NO,EL是矩形,MN,NO;因此,MN,NO的正方形和不可公度是矩形,MN,NO。"}]},{"id":"euclid-10-59.proof.6","contentId":"euclid-10-59","revisionId":"euclid-10-59@raw-f0a9a345d616d972","order":8,"kind":"proof_step","title":"证明 6","status":"raw_machine","contentHash":"7449cfaacc514f74e719cfdb6664b448c5945644c3ecbcf96fa51d6b982ba051","citations":[],"surfaces":[{"id":"heath-en","role":"source","language":"en","status":"source_transcription","text":"And each of them is medial, and MN, NO are incommensurable in square."},{"id":"machine-zh","role":"machine_translation","language":"zh-CN","status":"raw_machine","text":"每一个是中项无理线段,MN,NO 不可公度"}]},{"id":"euclid-10-59.proof.7","contentId":"euclid-10-59","revisionId":"euclid-10-59@raw-f0a9a345d616d972","order":9,"kind":"proof_step","title":"证明 7","status":"raw_machine","contentHash":"bd6194ff5eff85b86f28fc119c6030dae698dcf50d77eeb4e2ea06b95535054e","citations":["euclid-10-41"],"surfaces":[{"id":"heath-en","role":"source","language":"en","status":"source_transcription","text":"Therefore MO is the side of the sum of two medial areas [[X. 41](/principles/euclid-10-41)], and is the side of AC. Q. E. D."},{"id":"machine-zh","role":"machine_translation","language":"zh-CN","status":"raw_machine","text":"因此,MO地区是两个中项无理线段个地区之和,AC地区是Q地区。 [[X. 41](/principles/euclid-10-41)]"}]},{"id":"euclid-10-59.proof.8","contentId":"euclid-10-59","revisionId":"euclid-10-59@raw-f0a9a345d616d972","order":10,"kind":"proof_step","title":"证明 8","status":"raw_machine","contentHash":"321e467ccfb4b15adde277bd9c401be4c6f6812a5707a630aa5caecf00b0be10","citations":[],"surfaces":[{"id":"heath-en","role":"source","language":"en","status":"source_transcription","text":"[LEMMA. If a straight line be cut into unequal parts, the squares on the unequal parts are greater than twice the rectangle contained by the unequal parts."},{"id":"machine-zh","role":"machine_translation","language":"zh-CN","status":"raw_machine","text":"[LEMMA. 如果一条直线被分割成不平等部分,则不平等部分的正方形是不平等部分构成的矩形的两倍以上。"}]},{"id":"euclid-10-59.construction.3","contentId":"euclid-10-59","revisionId":"euclid-10-59@raw-f0a9a345d616d972","order":11,"kind":"construction","title":"作图与构造 3","status":"raw_machine","contentHash":"b6b049906d46ff60d1efd1657defb51bfe09a34cbc91a3411bb79c5148d6fd6b","citations":[],"surfaces":[{"id":"heath-en","role":"source","language":"en","status":"source_transcription","text":"Let AB be a straight line, and let it be cut into unequal parts at C, and let AC be the greater; I say that the squares on AC, CB are greater than twice the rectangle AC, CB."},{"id":"machine-zh","role":"machine_translation","language":"zh-CN","status":"raw_machine","text":"让AB线成为一条直线,C线切成不平分,AC线成为更大的;我说,AC线上的正方形是矩形的两倍,AC线是CB。"}]},{"id":"euclid-10-59.construction.4","contentId":"euclid-10-59","revisionId":"euclid-10-59@raw-f0a9a345d616d972","order":12,"kind":"construction","title":"作图与构造 4","status":"raw_machine","contentHash":"a2412e6a8d4bffd69a745665bc2fb91b32cf2acdc991c845242ac5d897fdf051","citations":[],"surfaces":[{"id":"heath-en","role":"source","language":"en","status":"source_transcription","text":"For let AB be bisected at D."},{"id":"machine-zh","role":"machine_translation","language":"zh-CN","status":"raw_machine","text":"AB在D上被拆分"}]},{"id":"euclid-10-59.proof.9","contentId":"euclid-10-59","revisionId":"euclid-10-59@raw-f0a9a345d616d972","order":13,"kind":"proof_step","title":"证明 9","status":"raw_machine","contentHash":"ccf7bc339715551b4b14047d3855f4cbac78217c97e24706dc280be62144ff42","citations":["euclid-2-5"],"surfaces":[{"id":"heath-en","role":"source","language":"en","status":"source_transcription","text":"Since then a straight line has been cut into equal parts at D, and into unequal parts at C, therefore the rectangle AC, CB together with the square on CD is equal to the square on AD, [[II. 5](/principles/euclid-2-5)] so that the rectangle AC, CB is less than double of the square on AD."},{"id":"machine-zh","role":"machine_translation","language":"zh-CN","status":"raw_machine","text":"从那时起,一条直线在D时被切成相等部分,而C时被切成不平等部分,因此,矩形 AC、CB和CD时的正方形和AD时的正方形和AD时的正方形和CB是相等部分,因此,矩形 AC、CB比AD时的正方形的两倍还少。 [[II. 5](/principles/euclid-2-5)]"}]},{"id":"euclid-10-59.conclusion","contentId":"euclid-10-59","revisionId":"euclid-10-59@raw-f0a9a345d616d972","order":14,"kind":"conclusion","title":"结论","status":"raw_machine","contentHash":"1d34feb8cc5072393a80321125e04ec2ce3f3ce6495e1a1a3f77ed21166cb01b","citations":["euclid-2-9"],"surfaces":[{"id":"heath-en","role":"source","language":"en","status":"source_transcription","text":"But the squares on AC, CB are double of the squares on AD, DC; [[II. 9](/principles/euclid-2-9)] therefore the squares on AC, CB are greater than twice the rectangle AC, CB. Q. E. D.]"},{"id":"machine-zh","role":"machine_translation","language":"zh-CN","status":"raw_machine","text":"但AC,CB的正方形是AD,DC的正方形的两倍;因此,AC,CB的正方形是矩形,CB的两倍以上。 ] [[II. 9](/principles/euclid-2-9)]"}]},{"id":"euclid-10-59.source","contentId":"euclid-10-59","revisionId":"euclid-10-59@raw-f0a9a345d616d972","order":15,"kind":"source","title":"来源、译者与开放许可","status":"raw_machine","contentHash":"93b12d90fea9c95f97166ee259e743fafcfb25e87aa1dc771615bba2b1e1914c","citations":[],"surfaces":[{"id":"provenance","role":"provenance_note","language":"en","status":"generated_metadata","text":"Perseus / Heath source: https://scaife.perseus.org/reader/urn:cts:greekLit:tlg1799.tlg001.perseus-eng2:10.prop_2.59/\nCorpus URN: urn:cts:greekLit:tlg1799.tlg001.perseus-eng2:10.prop_2.59\nCorpus SHA-256: ba12e2e47aec41f853ff32929a2d0467926f93280f1bf8870bda5016c29d143c\nLicense: CC BY-SA 4.0 (https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0/)"}]}],"outgoingEdges":[{"id":"edge:euclid-10-59:euclid-10-21:explicit","sourceContentId":"euclid-10-59","sourceBlockIds":["euclid-10-59.proof.2","euclid-10-59.proof.3"],"targetContentId":"euclid-10-21","type":"depends_on","provenance":{"kind":"explicit_source_reference","basis":"perseus_tei_ref","sourceUrn":"urn:cts:greekLit:tlg1799.tlg001.perseus-eng2:10.prop_2.59","sourceUrl":"https://scaife.perseus.org/reader/urn:cts:greekLit:tlg1799.tlg001.perseus-eng2:10.prop_2.59/","sourceLabel":"X. 21"}},{"id":"edge:euclid-10-59:euclid-10-13:explicit","sourceContentId":"euclid-10-59","sourceBlockIds":["euclid-10-59.proof.3"],"targetContentId":"euclid-10-13","type":"depends_on","provenance":{"kind":"explicit_source_reference","basis":"perseus_tei_ref","sourceUrn":"urn:cts:greekLit:tlg1799.tlg001.perseus-eng2:10.prop_2.59","sourceUrl":"https://scaife.perseus.org/reader/urn:cts:greekLit:tlg1799.tlg001.perseus-eng2:10.prop_2.59/","sourceLabel":"X. 13"}},{"id":"edge:euclid-10-59:euclid-6-1:exp